{"name":"Excelsior","hex":"#908b85","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Excelsior","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Candler County, Georgia.\nA township in Kalkaska County, Michigan.\nA city in Hennepin County, Minnesota. \nAn unincorporated community in Morgan County, Missouri.\nA ghost town in Atchison County, Missouri.\nA ghost town in Elko County, Nevada.\nA community in the city of War, McDowell County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Upshur County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in Webster County, West Virginia.\nAn unincorporated community in the town of Richwood, Richland County, Wisconsin.\nA town in Sauk County, Wisconsin.","An unincorporated community in Candler County, Georgia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Excelsior"}],"entries":[{"title":"Excelsior (Longfellow)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Excelsior\" is a short poem written in 1841 by American poet Henry Wadsworth Longfellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4a/Longfellow_Excelsior.png/330px-Longfellow_Excelsior.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excelsior_(Longfellow)"},{"title":"Bret Harte","blocks":[{"text":"Francis Brett Hart, known as Bret Harte, was an American short story writer and poet best remembered for short fiction featuring miners, gamblers, and other romantic figures of the California Gold Rush. In a career spanning more than four decades, he also wrote poetry, plays, lectures, book reviews, editorials, and magazine sketches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bret_Harte_by_Napoleon_Sarony.jpg/330px-Bret_Harte_by_Napoleon_Sarony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bret_Harte"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w